# Kodi verifies addons.xml against addons.xml.md5 before accepting the repo
# index. The digest is computed over the file's exact bytes, so the working
# tree, the commit, and what GitHub Pages serves must all agree on line
# endings. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) git would otherwise
# normalise these to LF on commit while the local copy stayed CRLF, making
# the published digest wrong and breaking the repo for every client.
#
# Force LF for everything textual, and mark binaries so git never touches
# them. See write_text_lf() in _repo_generator.py for the other half of this.

* text=auto eol=lf

addons.xml      text eol=lf
addons.xml.md5  text eol=lf
*.xml           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf

*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.xbt  binary
